Chapter: Fins

 FINS (Factory Interface Network Service), the command protocol of
 Omron SYSMAC PLCs -- common in packaging, material handling, and
 semiconductor equipment, and the Omron member of the PLC family beside
 EtherNet/IP, S7comm, and MELSEC. A command opens with a ten-octet
 header naming the information control field, the gateway count, and
 the destination and source network/node/unit route, then a service
 identifier; the command code and its parameters follow. Addresses are
 big-endian. Each builder returns a List Integer.

Section: Byte Helper

  fins-u16-be : Integer -> List Integer
  fins-u16-be (v) = [bit-and (bit-shru v 8) 255, bit-and v 255]

Section: Header

 The information control field 0x80 marks a command that requires a
 response; the gateway count is 0x02. Network, unit, and the reserved
 fields are zero for a direct local exchange, leaving the destination
 node, source node, and service id to the caller.

  fins-header : Integer, Integer, Integer -> List Integer
  fins-header (dest-node) (src-node) (sid) =
   [#80, #00, #02, #00, dest-node, #00, #00, src-node, #00, sid]

Section: Commands and Areas

  fins-cmd-mem-read : Integer = #0101
  fins-cmd-mem-write : Integer = #0102

  fins-area-cio : Integer = #B0
  fins-area-work : Integer = #B1
  fins-area-hold : Integer = #B2
  fins-area-dm : Integer = #82

Section: Memory Area Access

 A memory-area access names an area code, a two-octet beginning word
 address, a bit offset (zero for word access), and a two-octet item
 count. A write appends the word values.

  fins-mem-read : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> List Integer
  fins-mem-read (dest-node) (src-node) (sid) (area) (address) (count) =
   fins-header dest-node src-node sid & fins-u16-be fins-cmd-mem-read & [area] & fins-u16-be address & [#00] & fins-u16-be count

  fins-words-be : List Integer -> List Integer
  fins-words-be (words) = fins-words-loop words 0 (list-length words) []

  fins-words-loop : List Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  fins-words-loop (words) (i) (len) (acc) =
   if i >= len then acc
   else fins-words-loop words (i + 1) len (acc & fins-u16-be (list-at words i))

  fins-mem-write : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  fins-mem-write (dest-node) (src-node) (sid) (area) (address) (words) =
   fins-header dest-node src-node sid & fins-u16-be fins-cmd-mem-write & [area] & fins-u16-be address & [#00] & fins-u16-be (list-length words) & fins-words-be words
